$\begin{align}
\text{vertex's }x\text{-coordinate}&=\dfrac{(\goldD{1})+(\goldD{-4})}{2}
\\\\
&=\blueD{-\dfrac32}
\end{align}$

Now we can find the vertex's $y$-coordinate by evaluating $g\left(\blueD{-\dfrac32}\right)$:

$\begin{align}
g\left(\blueD{-\dfrac32}\right)&=\left(\blueD{-\dfrac32}\right)^2+3\left(\blueD{-\dfrac32}\right)-4
\\\\
&=\dfrac94-\dfrac92-4
\\\\
&=-\dfrac{25}{4}
\end{align}$
